{
  "dom_id": "step-17996",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "To raise the product of two numbers to a power, we can raise each number to that power, and then multiply. This is the **power of product rule for exponents**. \n\nTo demonstrate, let's simplify the expression $(5 \\times 3)^4$ by applying the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n(5\\times 3)^4=5^4\\times 3^4\n$$\n\n**Note:** The power of product rule for exponents is really just a quicker alternative to using repeated multiplication, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5\\times 3)^{4} & = \\\\ {{(5\\times 3)\\times (5\\times 3)\\times (5\\times 3)\\times (5\\times 3)}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{ copies}} & = \\\\ {{(5\\times 5\\times 5\\times 5)}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{ copies}}\\times {{(3\\times 3\\times 3\\times 3)}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{ copies}} & = \\\\ {5}^{4}\\times {3}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-17996\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"17996\" steptype=\"tutorial\" contentid=\"3272\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-17996\" class=\"stepAnchor\" name=\"step-1\">Introduction</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"17996\">?</div>\n            </div> \n\n            <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>To raise the product of two numbers to a power, we can raise each number to that power, and then multiply. This is the <strong>power of product rule for exponents</strong>. </p>\n<p>To demonstrate, let's simplify the expression <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"8.029ex\" height=\"3.009ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.838ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -934.9 3456.9 1295.7\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">(5